// Compose this frame's modelview handle: a fixed 18-degree downward tilt (so
// the terrain ahead and below is in view) plus a slow bank roll, then a
// translate that both lifts the camera to its cruise altitude and slides the
// world forward past it by `flown(t)` -- moving the world +Z is equivalent to
// the camera moving -Z, i.e. flying forward, the same "camera looks down -Z"
// convention demos/gl3d and demos/gl3dgame use. gl_mat_mul(a,b) applies b
// first, so this reads innermost-out: tilt, then bank, then translate.

build_view(int tick) {
  int rot = compose_tilt_bank(tick);
  int forward_matrix = forward_translate(tick);
  int view_matrix = gl_mat_mul(forward_matrix, rot);
} return int view_matrix;
